# A drag that takes the window to another display and back left AppKit's frame for it where it was:
# CraWindow skips AppKit's screen-layout adjustment for a move the window server reports
# (window-frame-adjust), and at a display crossing that adjustment is what records the moved frame.
# Every menu then opened away from the window: a <select>'s popup sat a display's width from its
# control (21 Nov 2026). frameAfterMove sends the window the report a drag onto another display
# sends; AppKit's frame must be the reported one afterwards. On a Mac with one display it can't cross.
budget rss=900 stalls50=40
pace 0.5

cra://open?url=${PAGE}
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://debug?frameAfterMove=1
expect-log frame after move: (recorded|one display)$
reject-log frame after move: stale
